{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HoefsmitRepGeneral","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HoefsmitRepGeneral","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SytAdmissible","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.hoefsmit_seminormal_rep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.hoefsmit_seminormal_rep","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HoefsmitRepGeneral.lean#L88-L144","doc":"**Hoefsmit seminormal representation, general shape `λ` — PROVED.**\n\nFor every partition `λ ⊢ N` there is a `d_λ`-dimensional representation\n`ρ_λ : H_N(q) →ₐ[ℝ] M_{d_λ}(ℝ)` which, when `d_λ ≥ 2`, sends at least one generator to a\n**non-scalar** matrix — so it is not the reducible `σ_i ↦ q·1` rep, and the statement is\nnon-vacuous.\n\n`q ≠ 0` together with `q ^ 2 ≠ 1` says exactly that `q` is not a root of unity over `ℝ`, which is\nthe genericity `[ram1997]`'s axial-distance formulas presuppose. Note this **admits negative `q`**:\nit is strictly weaker than `0 < q ∧ q ≠ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.card_le_one_of_cells_card_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.card_le_one_of_cells_card_zero","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HoefsmitRepGeneral.lean#L79-L86","doc":"A shape with no cells has at most one standard tableau: there is nothing to fill, so\n`syt_ext_on_cells` applies vacuously. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.card_shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.card_shape","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HoefsmitRepGeneral.lean#L60-L77","doc":"**`|shape λ| = N`** — a partition of `N` has `N` cells in its Young diagram.\n\nAdopted from the sibling PR #5282, which built it the right way: on\n`QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.card_eq_rowLens_sum`, already in the repo. I had written a\nstandalone `YoungDiagramCard.lean` re-proving that bridge because I probed Mathlib (where it is\ngenuinely absent) without grepping the corpus (where it is not). The duplicate is deleted. ","signatureChunk":0}]}